      },
      {
        "text": "One of the major obstacles to water and sanitation finance is project preparation",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Low institutional capacity",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "A local affair, sometimes removed from decision making centers",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Difficult political and economic conditions",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Scarcity of financial resources: users, taxpayers, markets",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Project preparation not given the key role",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Donors and multilaterals financial institutions must emphasize support for the early stage.",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "We at the IDB hope to approve on Monday a Project Preparation Fund with grants for capacity building and project preparation",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Donors should consider “debt for water swaps” as part of their official assistance.",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Both would leverage other funds: “teach them how to fish instead of giving them fish”",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Financial structures adapted to local realities",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Exploit all possibilities to maximize synergies between scarce resources: own labor, tariffs, donors, multilaterals, public and private resources",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "At one extreme, cooperatives, water microenterprises, municipal utilities",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "In the middle, management contracts, for operation, maintenance, collections, etc.",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "At the other extreme, full-fledged concessions",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Willingness to pay/local views",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Tariff sustainability",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Site and location",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Institutional capacity",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Fiscal space",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Legal framework",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Political risk",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Macroeconomic conditions",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Local conditions",
        "bold": true
      },
      {
        "text": "Project preparation and structuring may not be a source of funds, but can help bring funds and enhance the long term sustainability of water projects",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "All actors, all sources, all structures must be explored",
        "bold": false
      },
      {
        "text": "Antonio Vives",
        "bold": true
      },
      {
        "text": "Access to Finance for Local Governments",
        "bold": true
      },
      {
        "text": "IV World Water Forum",
        "bold": true
      },
      {
        "text": "March 17, 2006",
        "bold": true
      }
